{"name":"Afterlife","hex":"#d91fff","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"afterlife","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A conscious existence after death; a supernatural life that follows one's natural life, in some worldviews.","The place believed to be inhabited by people who have died."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/afterlife"}],"entries":[{"title":"Afterlife","blocks":[{"text":"The afterlife or life after death is a speculation concerning existence after death, in which the essential part of an individual's stream of consciousness or identity continues to exist after the death of their physical body. The surviving essential aspect varies between belief systems; it may be some partial element, or the entire soul or spirit, which carries with it one's personal identity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Idris_the_prophet.jpg/330px-Idris_the_prophet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afterlife","wikidata":"Q623282"},{"title":"Afterlife (Evanescence song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Afterlife\" is a song by American rock band Evanescence. It was released on 28 March 2025 by Netflix Music as a single for the soundtrack of the adult animated urban fantasy action series Devil May Cry. The song also appears on the band's sixth studio album, Sanctuary. It reached number 1 on the Billboard Mainstream Rock Airplay and Rock & Alternative Airplay charts in July 2025."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8b/Evanescence_-_Afterlife_%28song%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afterlife_(Evanescence_song)","wikidata":"Q138641407"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Traditional_bhavachakra_wall_mural_of_Yama_holding_the_wheel_of_life%2C_Buddha_pointing_the_way_out.jpg/500px-Tradition